On Tue, 14 Nov 2006, Nexos wrote:

[Please write below quoted text.]

> Korodzik wrote:
> > Whenever I begin a game, I'm stuck. I end up on a level without any
> > stairs. I check all the corridors and rooms, to no avail. Recently, I
> > began the game in a small 10x7 room without any doors. Why is this
> > happening?
> They may be hidden doors ; just use the search command 's' several
> times while next to a wall (you can also apply a stethoscope).
> The success rates depends (on the presence of a secret door) mainly on
> your character's intelligence.

It also depends on your luck, but in the beginning there are only few ways
to decrease luck; mainly killing peaceful creatures, or eating monsters of
your own race.

Typing "n10s" will let your character search up to 10 times, but
automatically stop if something is found. Searching applies to all
adjacent squares, so one such command covers at least three wall
positions.

